{
  "commit": "4e9338b4fb741523ea30ba99b895ec758b4befb3",
  "instructions": "Controls MiSTer FPGA retro-gaming hardware through Zaparoo Core and root SSH. In the gaming cabinet signal chain, the MiSTer FPGA acts as the Video and Audio Source feeding direct HDMI or analog RGB video into the AV Receiver (Onkyo) or TV (LG webOS). Game launch events trigger dynamic marquee updates on Pixelcade LED displays. Play tracking publishes real-time session events to Home Assistant via MQTT ('misterfpga/<host>/now_playing'). Call mister_get_status first: it lists each MiSTer by name and model, what it's playing, and its capabilities and limitations. Find games with mister_search_games or mister_play_history; launch them with mister_launch(game=<ref>). mister_launch refuses while a game is running: ask before ending one with mister_return_to_menu, since unsaved progress is lost. Pass host only when the call doesn't already say which MiSTer (a ref does).",
  "package": "misterfpga_mcp",
  "server": "misterfpga",
  "tools": [
    {
      "annotations": {
